The analysts also noted that SpaceX lifted its overall target from 10 gigawatts only two

00:05:34.057 --> 00:05:39.254
months after skeptics had questioned whether the earlier plan was even achievable. Standing

00:05:39.254 --> 00:05:44.434
up halls this fast from an engineering standpoint is less a trick of pouring concrete quicker

00:05:44.434 --> 00:05:50.254
than physics allows, and more a refusal to run the trades in single-file. Space X is opening

00:05:50.254 --> 00:05:55.034
several work fronts at once, and taking existing industrial buildings instead of empty dirt,

00:05:55.594 --> 00:05:59.214
so a lot of the civil sequence that usually sits on the calendar never starts.

00:05:59.954 --> 00:06:04.694
At gun range, foundation and structural steel began while site utilities were still being

00:06:04.694 --> 00:06:09.254
finished, which is the opposite of the usual rule that nothing vertical happens until the

00:06:09.254 --> 00:06:14.674
civil packages signed off. The same pattern at Starbase turned cleared land into simultaneous

00:06:14.674 --> 00:06:19.974
frame and roof erection within weeks, which moves the critical path onto material delivery

00:06:19.974 --> 00:06:25.734
and inspection holdpoints, rather than a parade of earthwork packages. Parallel work only

00:06:25.734 --> 00:06:30.754
holds if the design is frozen early and if the owner controls both the land and the supply chain.

00:06:31.394 --> 00:06:37.354
And SpaceX meets both tests. Conventional builds still wait on a 28-day concrete strength test

00:06:37.354 --> 00:06:42.574
before the next trade fully loads the slab, a cylinder test that has sat in the code since the

00:06:42.574 --> 00:06:50.294
early 1900s. Structural concrete itself comes in around 2,400 kg per cubic meter, so every extra

00:06:50.294 --> 00:06:56.014
week of formwork is mass sitting idle under a crane. Time on site is the cost the idiot index

00:06:56.014 --> 00:07:02.194
actually sees. On a back of envelope figure, a finished megawatt of powered, cooled hall can run on

00:07:02.194 --> 00:07:05.434
the order of 10 times the raw steel, copper, and concrete.

00:07:05.834 --> 00:07:11.674
That gap is not physics, it is calendar, cranes, inspectors, interest, and crews waiting

00:07:11.674 --> 00:07:12.794
on the previous trade.

00:07:13.414 --> 00:07:18.514
Cut occupancy in half and you attack that index directly, which is why it can fall faster

00:07:18.514 --> 00:07:20.854
than power or cooling limits alone would suggest.

00:07:21.614 --> 00:07:23.714
Cooling still has to obey thermodynamics.

00:07:24.354 --> 00:07:31.454
Modern halls often run at a power usage effectiveness of roughly 1.3, meaning about 30% of site electricity

00:07:31.454 --> 00:07:33.974
